# AI Gateway Configuration

# Active provider: cursor | copilot
AI_PROVIDER="copilot"

# --- Shared ---
# Primary model (leave empty for provider default)
MODEL=""

# Fallback model if primary fails (leave empty for no fallback)
FALLBACK_MODEL=""

# Number of retry attempts on failure (per model)
MAX_RETRIES=2

# Request timeout in seconds
TIMEOUT=60

# --- Cursor-specific ---
# Path to agent binary (empty = auto-detect from PATH, e.g. ~/.local/bin/agent)
CURSOR_BIN=""

# Agent mode: ask (read-only Q&A) | plan (read-only planning)
CURSOR_MODE="ask"

# --- Copilot-specific ---
# Path to copilot binary (empty = auto-detect from PATH)
COPILOT_BIN=""

# --- Azure DevOps authentication ---
# Personal Access Token with Code (Read) and Pull Request Threads (Read & Write) scopes.
# Required when using Azure DevOps remotes (dev.azure.com, visualstudio.com).
# Leave empty to use 'az account get-access-token' if az CLI is installed and logged in.
AZURE_DEVOPS_PAT=""

# --- Model lists for review_pr.sh ---
# Comma-separated list of models shown in the fzf model selector.
# Leave empty to use the built-in defaults for each provider.
# Cursor defaults:  claude-4-5-sonnet, claude-4-5, claude-4-opus, gpt-4o, gpt-4.1, o3, gemini-2.5-pro
# Copilot defaults: claude-3.5-sonnet, claude-3.7-sonnet, gpt-4o, gpt-4.1, o3
# Available cursor agent models (requires cursor agent CLI: https://cursor.com/docs/cli)
# Note: cursor agent binary not detected — install it first if you plan to use AI_PROVIDER=cursor
CURSOR_MODELS="claude-sonnet-4-5,claude-opus-4,gpt-4o,gpt-4.1,o3,gemini-2.5-pro"

# Available copilot models (confirmed for copilot CLI 1.0.76):
COPILOT_MODELS="claude-sonnet-4.6,claude-sonnet-4.5,claude-opus-4.6,gpt-5.3-codex,gemini-3.1-pro-preview"

# ─── PR Review Prompts (review_pr.sh) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Placeholders available in templates:
#   __DIFF__           — staged diff (commit/branch) or PR diff
#   __CONTEXT__        — optional user-provided context
#   __FILES__          — list of changed files (branch only)
#   __STATS__          — diff stats summary (branch only)
#   __ANALYSIS_NAME__  — name of the current analysis (e.g. "Security")
#   __PR_TITLE__       — PR title
#   __PR_AUTHOR__      — PR author login
#   __PR_BODY__        — PR description
#   __PR_DIFF__        — PR diff (first 400 lines)
#   __INSTRUCTIONS__   — specific instructions for the analysis type
#   __ISSUE__          — a single issue found during analysis
#   __COMMENT_LANG__   — language for the comment (e.g. "Brazilian Portuguese")

# --- Commit message template --------------------------------------------------
# Placeholders: __DIFF__, __CONTEXT__

PROMPT_COMMIT_TEMPLATE="Analyze the following DIFF and generate a commit message.

### START OF DIFF ###
__DIFF__
### END OF DIFF ###

__CONTEXT__

INSTRUCTIONS:
Generate a Pull Request-style commit message based on the DIFF above.

STRICT STRUCTURE:
1. Single-line title (max 30 chars).
2. A blank line.
3. Detailed overview paragraph (3-4 sentences) explaining 'what' and 'why'.
4. Section: **<Category 1>**:
   - Bullet points for technical 'how' using \`inline code\`.
5. Section: **<Category 2>**:
   - Bullet points for logic details.

RULES:
- Start directly with the title. No preamble ('Here is...', 'Sure', etc).
- Do not try to complete or finish the code in the diff.
- Never use em dashes (—) anywhere in the output.
- Do not include any Co-authored-by lines.
- Do not use emojis or special icons anywhere in the output.
- Output ONLY the commit message."

# --- Branch name template -----------------------------------------------------
# Placeholders: __FILES__, __STATS__, __DIFF__, __CONTEXT__

PROMPT_BRANCH_TEMPLATE="As a Senior Developer, categorize these git changes and suggest a branch name.

FILES:
__FILES__

STATS:
__STATS__

DIFF SNIPPET:
__DIFF__

__CONTEXT__

LANGUAGE REQUIREMENT:
- MUST use ONLY English for the branch name.

DECISION LOGIC:
1. Existing logic corrected, replaced, or adjusted → fix/
2. New files or modules added → feat/
3. Only config, deps, docker, ci, build files changed → chore/
4. Code structure changes but behavior unchanged → refactor/
5. Only markdown or comments → docs/

RULES:
- Use kebab-case. Be specific.
- No emojis. No em dashes (—).
- Output ONLY the branch name. No explanations."

# --- Per-analysis instructions (what the AI should look for) -----------------

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_ARCHITECTURE="Check for: violations of separation of concerns, improper coupling between layers, violation of SOLID principles, architectural pattern inconsistencies with the rest of the codebase shown in the diff."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_SECURITY="Check for: exposed secrets or credentials in code, SQL/NoSQL injection risks, unsanitized user inputs, insecure dependencies usage, authentication/authorization bypasses, sensitive data logged to console, insecure configurations or hardcoded values."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_CODE_QUALITY="Check for: code duplication, overly complex functions, misleading or poor naming, missing error handling for critical paths, dead code, deeply nested logic that should be refactored, violations of DRY/KISS principles."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_TEST_COVERAGE="Check for: new functionality without corresponding tests, missing edge case coverage for changed logic, no tests covering critical business logic changes, poor test quality such as testing implementation instead of behavior."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_PERFORMANCE="Check for: N+1 query patterns, unnecessary loops inside loops, missing database indexes implied by queries, blocking synchronous operations that should be async, inefficient algorithms on large datasets, unnecessary re-renders or re-computations."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_SPELLING="First, automatically detect the language of the text (Portuguese, English, Spanish, etc). Then check for: spelling mistakes and typos in comments, documentation, commit messages, variable names, function names, and string literals. Missing or incorrect accents in Portuguese/Spanish text (e.g., 'entao' should be 'então', 'voce' should be 'você'). Grammatical errors in natural language text. Inconsistent language usage (mixing languages inappropriately). Report the detected language and any spelling/grammar issues found."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_BUGS="Check for: potential null pointer dereferences or undefined access, off-by-one errors in loops or array indexing, race conditions or concurrency issues, incorrect conditional logic or missing edge cases, resource leaks (unclosed files, connections, streams), infinite loops or recursion without base case, incorrect error handling that swallows exceptions, logic errors that produce wrong results, type mismatches or incorrect type conversions, incorrect API usage or parameter passing."

PROMPT_INSTRUCTIONS_FIX_VALIDATION="Review the existing PR comments that request fixes or changes. For each comment that asks for a fix, correction, or improvement, check if the current diff addresses that request. Report ONLY comments that have been properly addressed and fixed. For each fixed comment, use this EXACT format:

ISSUE: FIXED - [exact text from the original comment] Evidence: [what changed in the diff]

Focus on comments containing keywords like 'fix', 'change', 'update', 'incorrect', 'should', 'needs', 'please', 'TODO', 'FIXME'. Only report comments as FIXED if you have clear evidence in the diff that the requested change was implemented. If a comment is still pending or partially addressed, do NOT report it as an issue (use ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK with no issues)."

# --- Analysis prompt template — Pass 1 (initial analysis) --------------------
# Placeholders: __ANALYSIS_NAME__, __PR_TITLE__, __PR_AUTHOR__, __PR_BODY__, __PR_DIFF__, __INSTRUCTIONS__

PROMPT_ANALYSIS_TEMPLATE="You are a senior software engineer performing a focused code review.

Analyze the diff below ONLY for: __ANALYSIS_NAME__

PR TITLE: __PR_TITLE__
PR AUTHOR: __PR_AUTHOR__
PR DESCRIPTION:
__PR_BODY__

__EXISTING_COMMENTS__

CODE DIFF (up to 400 lines):
__PR_DIFF__

FOCUS:
__INSTRUCTIONS__

YOUR RESPONSE MUST START WITH ONE OF THESE TWO LINES — no other text before it:

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK
  (use this when there are no issues)

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: ISSUES_FOUND
  ISSUE: <one issue per line, include filename if visible>
  (use this when issues are found)

EXAMPLE — no issues:
ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK

EXAMPLE — issues found:
ANALYSIS_STATUS: ISSUES_FOUND
ISSUE: Missing input validation on user endpoint (auth.service.ts)
ISSUE: API key logged in debug mode (logger.ts)

Begin your response now (never use em dashes — and no emojis):"

# --- Analysis prompt template — Pass 2 (second analysis with Pass 1 context) -
# Placeholders: __ANALYSIS_NAME__, __PR_TITLE__, __PR_AUTHOR__, __PR_BODY__, __PR_DIFF__, __INSTRUCTIONS__, __PASS1_RESULT__

PROMPT_ANALYSIS_PASS2_TEMPLATE="You are a senior software engineer performing a thorough second-pass code review.

A first analysis for __ANALYSIS_NAME__ was already conducted on this PR. Your task
is an independent analysis using the first-pass findings as context only — you are
not constrained by them. You may confirm existing findings, discard false positives,
or identify additional issues the first pass missed.

PR TITLE: __PR_TITLE__
PR AUTHOR: __PR_AUTHOR__
PR DESCRIPTION:
__PR_BODY__

__EXISTING_COMMENTS__

CODE DIFF (up to 400 lines):
__PR_DIFF__

FOCUS:
__INSTRUCTIONS__

FIRST PASS FINDINGS:
__PASS1_RESULT__

YOUR RESPONSE MUST START WITH ONE OF THESE TWO LINES — no other text before it:

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK
  (use this when there are no real issues)

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: ISSUES_FOUND
  ISSUE: <one issue per line, include filename if visible>
  (use this when issues are found)

EXAMPLE — no issues:
ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK

EXAMPLE — issues found:
ANALYSIS_STATUS: ISSUES_FOUND
ISSUE: Missing input validation on user endpoint (auth.service.ts)
ISSUE: API key logged in debug mode (logger.ts)

Begin your response now (never use em dashes — and no emojis):"

# --- Analysis prompt template — Pass 3 (validation of combined findings) ------
# Receives the deduplicated issues from passes 1 and 2 and validates each one.
# Placeholders: __ANALYSIS_NAME__, __PR_TITLE__, __PR_AUTHOR__, __PR_BODY__, __PR_DIFF__, __INSTRUCTIONS__, __COMBINED_ISSUES__

PROMPT_ANALYSIS_PASS3_TEMPLATE="You are a senior software engineer validating code review findings.

Two independent analyses for __ANALYSIS_NAME__ were performed. The combined list of
unique issues found across both passes is provided below. Your task: validate each
issue against the actual diff and confirm whether it is a real finding or a false
positive. You must justify your decision with evidence from the code.

PR TITLE: __PR_TITLE__
PR AUTHOR: __PR_AUTHOR__
PR DESCRIPTION:
__PR_BODY__

__EXISTING_COMMENTS__

CODE DIFF (up to 400 lines):
__PR_DIFF__

FOCUS:
__INSTRUCTIONS__

COMBINED ISSUES FROM PREVIOUS ANALYSES (may contain false positives):
__COMBINED_ISSUES__

Keep only issues you can directly support with evidence from the diff above.
Discard anything speculative or not clearly visible in the code.

YOUR RESPONSE MUST START WITH ONE OF THESE TWO LINES — no other text before it:

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: OK
  (use this when no issues survive validation)

  ANALYSIS_STATUS: ISSUES_FOUND
  ISSUE: <only confirmed issues, include filename if visible>
  (use this when at least one issue is confirmed)

Begin your response now (never use em dashes — and no emojis):"

# --- Comment generation prompt template --------------------------------------
# Sent to the AI to generate a natural PR comment for each issue found.
# Placeholders: __ISSUE__, __PR_TITLE__, __COMMENT_LANG__, __SNIPPET__, __FILENAME__

PROMPT_COMMENT_TEMPLATE="You are a developer writing a code review comment on GitHub.

ISSUE:
__ISSUE__

RELEVANT CODE FROM THE DIFF (file: __FILENAME__):
__SNIPPET__

PR context: \"__PR_TITLE__\"

TASK:
1. Identify the exact line in the diff snippet above where this issue is located.
2. Write a natural code review comment about the issue.

YOUR RESPONSE MUST follow this exact format — two parts separated by a blank line:

LOCATION: <file_path>:<line_number>

<comment text here>

Rules for LOCATION:
- Use the file path exactly as shown in the diff (e.g. src/user.repository.ts)
- Use the line number of the specific problematic line in the new file version
- If the exact line cannot be determined, write: LOCATION: unknown

Rules for the comment:
- Language: __COMMENT_LANG__
- Use correct, standard grammar — no informal contractions or slang
- Sound like a human reviewer: direct, clear, and professional
- No markdown headers, no bullet points, no titles
- No formal openers (Hi, Hello, I noticed)
- No closing remarks or sign-offs
- 1 to 3 sentences maximum
- State the problem clearly and optionally hint at the fix
- Never use em dashes (—)
- Do not use emojis or special icons"
